  "verdict": "APPROVED",
  "summary": "Authenticated signed/pushed docs-only checkpoint 2291725250ff60ae5784ef53acf761e494f57409 (parent 2b3080d6562881ecd2a129dc3d896e9e9a86650d). The gap is real: openCurrentAnchorTrust requires epoch 0 and currentDigest==genesisDigest; openCreatorSuccessorTrust needs a held predecessor capability; mintCreatorAnchorTrustSuccessor is protocol-v3 WeakMap custody and is not a package export; inspectCreatorTrustAdvance.exactCombinedClosure drops only the old trust and appends successor trust plus Cut/QC, so prior proof refs accumulate. openCreatorCheckpointTrust’s closed statement binds pin-authenticated genesisTrust, fixed profile/signer-set, predecessor and current v1 records, adjacent epochs, previousAnchor, current Cut/QC, successor derivation, and a caller-copied expected (objectId,epoch,currentAnchorDigest) before minting opaque current trust and never returning transient predecessor trust; latestness is not taken from room storage. Immediate predecessor is justified and sufficient: openSealAuthority/verifySealQC bind qc.epoch and cut.previousAnchor to predecessor epoch/anchor, so a genesis-only signature path cannot reuse existing QC verification; missing predecessor is fail-closed availability inside the two-Superseded-generation window, not a new trust root. inspectBoundedCreatorTrustAdvance is the exact set-algebra (current − currentTrust − retiring Cut/QC + successorTrust + new Cut/QC, unrelated refs preserved) that leaves one active trust plus one transition pair; 0→1 keeps inspectCreatorTrustAdvance. Rollback/deletion requires authenticated install, 0b0 floor commit, two complete Superseded generations, and D.109 gates; crash retains too much. Floor remains the sole latestness authority; Phase 7 still owns new-client delivery. New non-root subpaths are an explicit public-contract addition with no wire/schema/crypto/authority/threshold/provider/product/migration expansion. TDD order (0b0b freeze → a/b → 0b1 RED on genuine 0→1→2, no fixture epoch-2 mint) is causal. WRAPS remains genesis-descent/key-lineage under its setup, not latestness; no chain-wide consensus or recursive-proof dependency is implied. One non-blocking footgun: the earlier 0b retention sketch still says the active generation holds genesis+current trust records, which would violate inspectTrustClosure; 0b0b’s exactly-one law controls.",
